# This is a RETARGET, not a fix. `SlideAutofit`'s twelve `constScaleLevels` rows and its 0.250
# floor are a correct, deliberate port of LibreOffice **26.2.4.2** (round slides-r52,
# `dotnet/probes/slides-r52/results.md`). The `soffice` installed in THIS container, and the one
# that wrote every reference PDF under /data/bench/lo/, is **24.2.7.2** — whose autofit answers a
# 2.5 per-cent font grid with no floor, measured on 36 probe decks in
# `/data/bench/fix-lanes/L5-slides/probe/fit/`.
#
# Applying this makes the tree agree with THIS sweep's reference and disagree with the project's.
# It will fail `SlideAutofitTests`, `SlideMarkerScaleTests` and the two
# `SlideAutofit*ComparisonTests` fidelity suites, all of which pin 26.2.4.2 answers, and those
# would have to move with it. The alternative — re-render the reference bank at 26.2.4.2 — leaves
# the tree alone and re-scores 25 of this lane's 35 documents instead. That choice is above this
# lane; see findings.md, root cause A.
